WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:10.232
Alice walked around the March Hare's house until she spotted a table under a tree.

2
00:00:10.233 --> 00:00:13.826
The March Hare and the Hatter were having tea.

3
00:00:13.827 --> 00:00:18.065
A dormouse sat between them, fast asleep.

4
00:00:18.066 --> 00:00:22.897
The other two rested their elbows on him as they chatted.

5
00:00:22.898 --> 00:00:28.436
Although the table was large, all three were crowded at one end.

6
00:00:28.437 --> 00:00:35.917
As Alice approached, the Hatter and the March Hare jumped up.

7
00:00:35.918 --> 00:00:45.018
"There's no room for you!" they cried. "No room at all!"

8
00:00:45.019 --> 00:00:52.198
"Nonsense! There's plenty of room."

9
00:00:52.199 --> 00:00:57.657
Alice sat down in an armchair at the other end of the table.

10
00:00:57.658 --> 00:01:02.554
Sighing, the Hatter and the March Hare sat down again.

11
00:01:02.555 --> 00:01:06.915
"Have some juice," the March Hare said.

12
00:01:06.916 --> 00:01:09.201
Alice looked around the table.

13
00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:13.275
"I see tea, but I don't see any juice."

14
00:01:13.276 --> 00:01:18.766
"That's because there isn't any," the March Hare said.

15
00:01:18.767 --> 00:01:24.415
"Then it wasn't very nice of you to offer it." Alice felt impatient.

16
00:01:24.416 --> 00:01:31.878
"It wasn't very nice of you to sit down without being invited," the March Hare said. "You

17
00:01:31.879 --> 00:01:36.069
have plenty of room here," Alice said. All

18
00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:41.928
this time the Hatter had been silently studying Alice. "You

19
00:01:41.929 --> 00:01:49.421
need a haircut," he said. "And

20
00:01:49.422 --> 00:01:56.717
you need to stop making personal comments!" Alice scolded him. She

21
00:01:56.718 --> 00:02:01.765
couldn't believe how rude everyone was in this strange land. The

22
00:02:01.766 --> 00:02:06.122
Hatter took his watch from his pocket and studied it. He

23
00:02:06.123 --> 00:02:09.767
shook the watch and held it to his ear. "What

24
00:02:09.768 --> 00:02:13.203
day of the month is it?" he asked Alice. She

25
00:02:13.204 --> 00:02:15.669
thought for a moment. "The

26
00:02:15.670 --> 00:02:17.844
fourth." The

27
00:02:17.845 --> 00:02:24.047
Hatter sighed. "My watch is off by two days." He

28
00:02:24.048 --> 00:02:26.847
gave the March Hare an angry look. "I

29
00:02:26.848 --> 00:02:30.711
told you that butter wouldn't fix it." "But

30
00:02:30.712 --> 00:02:36.063
I used the best kind of butter," the March Hare said. "Yes,

31
00:02:36.064 --> 00:02:41.517
but you shouldn't have used the bread knife to spread it inside my watch. Some

32
00:02:41.518 --> 00:02:46.099
bread crumbs obviously got in as well." The

33
00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:50.916
March Hare took the watch and looked at it gloomily. Then

34
00:02:50.917 --> 00:02:55.383
he dipped it into his tea and checked it again. The

35
00:02:55.384 --> 00:03:00.197
watch still didn't work. Alice

36
00:03:00.198 --> 00:03:03.487
got up and peered over his shoulder. "What

37
00:03:03.488 --> 00:03:05.862
a strange watch! It

38
00:03:05.863 --> 00:03:09.778
tells the day of the month but not the hour." "Why

39
00:03:09.779 --> 00:03:12.376
should it?" the Hatter said. "Does

40
00:03:12.377 --> 00:03:15.905
your watch tell you what year it is?" "Of

41
00:03:15.906 --> 00:03:18.769
course not," Alice said. Suddenly

42
00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:22.046
the Dormouse woke up. "That's

43
00:03:22.047 --> 00:03:30.636
what I was going to say!" he said, and immediately went back to sleep. Alice

44
00:03:30.637 --> 00:03:34.807
sat back down at the other end of the table. "This

45
00:03:34.808 --> 00:03:37.397
conversation makes no sense. I

46
00:03:37.398 --> 00:03:42.101
have better things to do with my time than sit here and waste it." The

47
00:03:42.102 --> 00:03:46.160
Hatter looked down his nose at Alice. "Time

48
00:03:46.161 --> 00:03:50.604
is a he , not an it

49
00:03:50.605 --> 00:03:53.664
." "I don't understand," Alice said.

50
00:03:53.665 --> 00:03:56.928
"Of course you don't," the Hatter said.

51
00:03:56.929 --> 00:04:00.517
"I bet you've never even spoken to Time.

52
00:04:00.518 --> 00:04:05.045
If you're friendly with him, he'll do almost anything you ask."

53
00:04:05.046 --> 00:04:10.236
Alice leaned forward, full of curiosity. "Like what?"

54
00:04:10.237 --> 00:04:17.025
"Let's say it's nine o'clock in the morning, and you're supposed to start your lessons.

55
00:04:17.026 --> 00:04:20.514
You could whisper to Time.

56
00:04:20.515 --> 00:04:26.026
And suddenly it would be one o'clock and time for lunch."

57
00:04:26.027 --> 00:04:29.316
"Oh, that would be wonderful!" Alice said.

58
00:04:29.317 --> 00:04:31.519
"Are you friendly with Time?"

59
00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:33.795
The Hatter looked sad.

60
00:04:33.796 --> 00:04:41.365
"Not anymore. I was singing at a concert given by the Queen of Hearts.

61
00:04:41.366 --> 00:04:48.191
I'd just begun when the Queen shouted, 'Stop! You're murdering the time!'"

62
00:04:48.192 --> 00:04:50.943
The Dormouse suddenly woke up again.

63
00:04:50.944 --> 00:04:57.995
"The Queen was mad because the Hatter wasn't keeping the beat."

64
00:04:57.996 --> 00:05:01.555
The Hatter nodded sadly.

65
00:05:01.556 --> 00:05:05.307
"But Time thought I wanted to murder him!

66
00:05:05.308 --> 00:05:10.125
And now he won't do a thing for me.

67
00:05:10.126 --> 00:05:17.247
It's always six o'clock!"

